<title>INDIA: India SEBI sets norms for off-market deals.</title>
<headline>India SEBI sets norms for off-market deals.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) on Wednesday set norms for &quot;negotiated deals&quot; or off-market transactions.</p>
<p>&quot;It has been decided that with effect from June 1, 1997 all negotiated deals ... would compulsorily result in delivery of securities,&quot; the market watchdog said in a statement after a day-long meeting with officials of 22 exchanges.</p>
<p>&quot;This would eliminate some of the possible malpractices,&quot; it said, without elaborating.</p>
<p>Presently, such negotiated deals are squared-up by market players, brokers said.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
